    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0520" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/>

                <head>253. Memorandum From Robert W.
                        Komer of the National Security Council Staff to President
                        Kennedy<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d253-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-02-16">February 16,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Here is a brief updating on our India and Kashmir enterprise. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">2 lines of source text not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <p>DOD is also embarking upon an overt, but
                    hopefully unpublicized Special Forces training effort which will involve 35 of
                    our people initially and perhaps more later.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d253-f2"/></p>
                <p>We still see little evidence that Peiping is planning any spring attack; indeed
                    the pace of Indian preparations suggests that they don’t really expect one
                    either.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">R. W.
                                Komer</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d253-a1.xml" xpointer="d253-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d253-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d253-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, India,
                    General, 2/14/63-2/17/63. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d253-f2" n="1" xml:id="d253-f2-content">
                <p>The reference is to assistance in training units of the Indian armed forces in
                    guerrilla tactics and unconventional warfare. Documentation on this training
                    program is in Department of State, Central Files 791.5 and DEF 7 INDIA-US)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
